1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,722
OK,

2
00:00:00,722 --> 00:00:04,210
so we've been looking at the attitudes of various social

3
00:00:04,210 --> 00:00:09,482
and cultural groups towards the management of their personal finances-how important they feel it

4
00:00:09,482 --> 00:00:10,344
is to save money,

5
00:00:10,344 --> 00:00:12,970
and what they save their money for.

6
00:00:12,970 --> 00:00:16,500
One aspect that we haven't yet considered is gender.

7
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:20,833
So if we consider gender issues we're basically asking whether men

8
00:00:20,833 --> 00:00:23,562
and women have different attitudes towards saving money,

9
00:00:23,562 --> 00:00:26,350
and whether they save money for different things.

10
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:33,984
Back in 1928 the British writer George Bernard Shaw wrote in his Intelligent Women's Guide to Socialism

11
00:00:33,984 --> 00:00:39,174
and Capitalism that 'A man is supposed to understand politics, economics and finance

12
00:00:39,174 --> 00:00:42,500
and is therefore unwilling to accept essential instruction.'

13
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:48,700
He also said, 'A woman, having fewer pretensions, is far more willing to learn'.

14
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:53,554
Now, though these days people might question a lot of the assumptions contained in

15
00:00:53,554 --> 00:01:00,172
those statements, recent research does suggest that there are some quite fundamental differences between men

16
00:01:00,172 --> 00:01:03,000
and women in their attitudes to economic matters.

17
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:08,060
Let's look at what men and women actually save for.

18
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:14,078
Research studies of women in North America have found that women are far more

19
00:01:14,078 --> 00:01:18,713
likely to save for their children's education and they are also more likely to

20
00:01:18,713 --> 00:01:21,120
save up in order to buy a house one day.

21
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:26,538
The same studies have found that men, on the other hand, tend to save

22
00:01:26,538 --> 00:01:27,261
for a car,

23
00:01:27,261 --> 00:01:32,198
which by the way takes a surprisingly large amount of the household budget in

24
00:01:32,198 --> 00:01:32,920
North America.

25
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:39,156
But the other main priority for men when saving money is their retirement.

26
00:01:39,156 --> 00:01:43,049
When they're earning, they're far more likely to put money aside for their old

27
00:01:43,049 --> 00:01:44,550
age than women are.

28
00:01:44,550 --> 00:01:46,606
Now this is rather disturbing,

29
00:01:46,606 --> 00:01:52,364
because in fact the need for women to save for their old age is

30
00:01:52,364 --> 00:01:54,420
far greater than for men.

31
00:01:54,420 --> 00:01:57,040
Let's consider this for a moment.

32
00:01:57,040 --> 00:02:01,764
To start with, it is a fact that throughout the world, women are likely

33
00:02:01,764 --> 00:02:04,126
to live many years longer than men,

34
00:02:04,126 --> 00:02:07,500
so they need money to support them during this time.

35
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:12,087
Since women are likely to be the ones left without a partner in old

36
00:02:12,087 --> 00:02:15,364
age, they may therefore have to pay for nursing care,

37
00:02:15,364 --> 00:02:18,640
because they don't have a spouse to look after them.

38
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:25,005
Furthermore the high divorce rates in North America are creating a poverty cycle for

39
00:02:25,005 --> 00:02:25,460
women.

40
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:31,688
It is the divorced women who will most often have to look after the children

41
00:02:31,688 --> 00:02:37,500
and thus they need more money to look after not just themselves but others.

42
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:43,610
So what can be done about this situation?

43
00:02:43,610 --> 00:02:49,051
The population in North America is likely to contain an increasing number of elderly

44
00:02:49,051 --> 00:02:49,440
women.

45
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:54,813
The research indicates that at present for women it takes a crisis to make

46
00:02:54,813 --> 00:02:57,500
them think about their future financial situation.

47
00:02:57,500 --> 00:03:02,596
But of course this is the very worst time for anyone to make important

48
00:03:02,596 --> 00:03:02,960
decisions.

49
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:09,310
Women today need to look ahead, think ahead-not wait until they're under pressure.

50
00:03:09,310 --> 00:03:14,351
Even women in their early twenties need to think about pensions, for example,

51
00:03:14,351 --> 00:03:19,779
and with increasing numbers of women in professional positions there are signs that this

52
00:03:19,779 --> 00:03:21,330
is beginning to happen.

53
00:03:21,330 --> 00:03:27,556
Then research also suggests that women avoid dealing effectively with their economic situation

54
00:03:27,556 --> 00:03:30,430
because of a lack of confidence.

55
00:03:30,430 --> 00:03:36,042
The best way for them to overcome this is by getting themselves properly informed

56
00:03:36,042 --> 00:03:39,650
so they are less dependent on other people's advice.

57
00:03:39,650 --> 00:03:44,260
A number of initiatives have been set up to help them do this.

58
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:50,202
This College, for example, is one of the educational institutions which offers night classes

59
00:03:50,202 --> 00:03:51,476
in Money Management,

60
00:03:51,476 --> 00:03:55,720
and increasing numbers of women are enrolling on such courses.

61
00:03:55,720 --> 00:04:00,110
Here, they can be given advice on different ways of saving.

62
00:04:00,110 --> 00:04:05,297
Many women are unwilling to invest in stocks and shares, for instance,

63
00:04:05,297 --> 00:04:07,890
but these can be extremely profitable.

64
00:04:07,890 --> 00:04:15,599
It is usually advised that at least 70% of a person's savings should be in low-risk investments

65
00:04:15,599 --> 00:04:21,040
but for the rest, financial advisors often advise taking some well-informed risks.

66
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:25,319
Initiatives such as this can give women the economic skills

67
00:04:25,319 --> 00:04:29,170
and knowledge they need for a comfortable, independent retirement.

68
00:04:29,170 --> 00:04:35,234
The increasing proportion of elderly women in the population is likely to have other

69
00:04:35,234 --> 00:04:36,100
economic consequences...
